      # v0.14-U (2026-05-18): Layer 41 — substrate problem-
      # solving capability inventory.
      #
      # Owner directive: "pnixc-meta 의 지능이 아직 문제풀이 능력
      # 준비가 안 되어있다면 그것을 우선 끌어올려야겠지?"
      #
      # This layer answers the question honestly. Before
      # claiming freecat-cli is a "코딩 에이전트" we need a
      # measured baseline of what the substrate CAN deterministi-
      # cally solve (no hardcoded answers, only owner-law'd
      # lifecycle), what it CANNOT, and where the production-
      # wire gap is. Future capability upgrades pin against this
      # baseline so we can measure whether they actually moved
      # the needle.
      #
      # Four lanes enumerated. Each lane row carries:
      #   lane_name
      #   can_solve_now    (list of concrete capability strings —
      #                     each phrasing what type of problem
      #                     the substrate routes to a deterministic
      #                     solver, NOT what scope it imagines)
      #   cannot_solve_now (list of honest-gap capability strings)
      #   production_wire_status (one of:
      #     "wired-to-doghouse-utterance-path",
      #     "substrate-only-not-wired-to-utterance-path",
      #     "substrate-only-cargo-test-only")
      #   primary_solver_owner  (path of the owner .px file)
      #   rust_body_handoff_count (int — number of plate boundary
      #                            crossings that actually call
      #                            Rust execution)
      #
      # Honest scope:
      #   - Cannot-solve lists are intentionally precise. "No
      #     general code generation" is honest; "no LLM" is also
      #     honest (substrate axiom).
      #   - production_wire_status surfaces the gap the owner
      #     pointed at: substrate has math/coding capabilities,
      #     but doghouse utterance path does NOT currently
      #     dispatch into them (only the capabilities read-model
      #     in pnix-coding-agent::run_capabilities mentions the
      #     lifter inventory).
      #   - Lists are *snapshot at v0.14-U* — when transforms are
      #     added (e.g. P4 remove-unused-import Rust body), the
      #     row must be updated in the same slice that lands the
      #     transform; ratchet pins the count so silent drift
      #     fails.
      substrate_problem_solving_inventory = {
        lanes = [
          {
            lane_name = "math-conjecture";
            can_solve_now = [
